<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_11.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Frost Death Knight Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>As a Frost Death Knight, you generally want trinkets that yield the highest amount of Strength as possible, as this is your most precious Stat due to multiple modifiers.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Frost Death Knights typically want two passive trinkets, as they can be used in conjunction with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>, granting the highest amount of Strength possible. Since every single damage-dealing ability of a Death Knight scales with Strength, it is also your most desirable Stat by far. <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105111/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> - This trinket is by far our best option for Phase 5, particularly as we approach full BIS. It amplifies our haste and mastery by 9% (when fully upgraded) and increases our critical strike damage by the same amount. On top of that, it also has a strength proc. This proc effect has an internal cooldown (ICD), unlike most other trinkets this tier.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105134/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> - This is your second-best alternative in Phase 5. Despite Frost Death Knights not valuing crit greatly, it still has great utility, especially on pull, where you're most likely to proc the trinket along with other offensive cooldowns.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104993/evil-eye-of-galakras">
<img alt="Evil Eye of Galakras" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Evil Eye of Galakras</span></a> - This trinket decreases the cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=42650/army-of-the-dead">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_armyofthedead.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Army of the Dead</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=47568/empower-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Empower Rune Weapon</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=51271/pillar-of-frost">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_deathknight_pillaroffrost.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pillar of Frost</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=77575/outbreak">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathvortex.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Outbreak</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48792/icebound-fortitude">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_iceboundfortitude.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icebound Fortitude</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48707/anti-magic-shell">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Anti-Magic Shell</span></a> by up to 50% when fully upgraded. One aspect often overlooked is the Runic Power generation value of the shorter cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48707/anti-magic-shell">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Anti-Magic Shell</span></a>, particularly when combined with the new <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146648/glyph-of-regenerative-magic">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Regenerative Magic</span></a> for this phase. This trinket is good, but not as valuable to Frost Death Knights as the other strength-based DPS classes.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=103989/alacrity-of-xuen">
<img alt="Alacrity of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_tigergodcub.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alacrity of Xuen</span></a> - This is a solid alternative, obtainable from the Timeless Isle. The trinkets from the celestial vendor still outperform this trinket.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104961/fusion-fire-core">
<img alt="Fusion-Fire Core" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion-Fire Core</span></a> - This is a niche trinket option that is only good in cleave/<wbr/>AOE environments. Very few fights value AOE damage highly, but may find good use cases depending on your raid composition.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">There are currently no active trinkets worth considering for Frost Death Knights.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
